    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine today is anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (71.91) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.76), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs north of 4.40. **Kyle Tucker** is our strongest play; he faces a sub-elite arm in Phillips and maintains an ideal batting order slot, making him a prime candidate to anchor both power and counting stats. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leverages his position against Bradish to push into the 70s, despite a slight drag from his dynamic platoon splits. While we are emphasizing stolen bases due to the league\u2019s scarcity, the core value today lies in these two mashers effectively neutralizing their respective matchups to provide high-floor production.\n\nStrategy-wise, the team is leaning into platoon advantages and lineup placement. **Josh Jung** (62.01) is a high-value start today, capitalizing on a significant boost from Pfaadt\u2019s 4.49 xERA and a favorable spot in the order. Meanwhile, **Heliot Ramos** (59.44) and **Gunnar Henderson** (59.63) hover just under the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold but remain essential for their capacity to produce across multiple categories; **Gunnar Henderson** is particularly bolstered by his dynamic platoon matchup against Miles. Our most difficult decision was keeping **Coby Mayo** (38.79) on the bench. He fell just short of the 40-point floor required for a start, as the optimizer heavily penalized his profile against Miles' SP skill metrics, ultimately prioritizing the higher efficiency ratings of our starting infielders.\n\nWe are monitoring the risk profile of **Jackson Merrill** (44.29) closely; while he receives a +5% bump due to wind conditions, his matchup against Perdomo remains a drag on his efficiency. Conversely, **Henry Bolte** (50.15) benefits from a 10% park factor surge, though the R/R matchup against Bryan Woo keeps his ceiling contained. With **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** unavailable due to IL or rest, the current lineup reflects our most effective rotation to maximize daily R, HR, and RBI production while balancing the imperative to preserve our game caps.",
